00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:08.810 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  Kingdom Hearts 3 is a game preoccupied  with fanservice and struggled to stay  coherent under the weight of its own  convoluted law but it's also everything  fans love about the series a thrilling  action RPG that celebrates Disney and  Pixar all the while ensuring themes of  friendship heroism and pure hearted  goodness shine bright at times those  themes can be difficult to discern  particularly when the game is intent on  telling the grander story of Kingdom  Hearts as opposed to the smaller tale  centered around Disney's iconic  characters or Sora's innocent idealism  given that it's the concluding chapter  in a massive story arc it can't be  followed for having this fixation but  the execution is frustrating nonetheless  Kingdom Hearts 3 is bogged down in the  finer details of its law so much so that  for all but the most clued in fans it  can be difficult to get a sense of what  our 3 main heroes are actually trying to  accomplish as broadus the story of  Kingdom Hearts 3 involves Sora Donald  and Goofy preparing for an upcoming war  against the forces of darkness by  gathering the guardians of light  this is oversimplification to its most  extreme but to delve into the finer  details would require lengthy  explanations of numerous confounding  concepts and characters is undoubtedly  messy but for fans who have committed to  playing all the games and been studious  enough to join the dots along the way it  makes sense for those that aren't as  well versed in Kingdom Hearts the  essentials of the story aren't laid out  nearly as clear as they need to be the  writing largely makes proceedings even  harder to follow the villains in  particular many of which are members of  organization 13 spout inane lines that  are purposefully vague presumably this  was to build mystery by only serves to  muddy motivations and further obscure  the crux of the story otherwise they're  delivering cheesy dialogue that feels  are ordered with the sincere melodrama  happening around them this is a shame  because at its core Kingdom Hearts free  is a heartfelt tale of enduring  friendship and the narrative is that is  strongest when it narrows its focus to  just this Sora Donald and Goofy are an  endearing trio they adventures through  the Disney and Pixar worlds as well as  the interactions they have with the  characters within them are a reminder  that beneath the torturous law are  smaller stories that resonate  by keeping the bigger Keyblade war in  the periphery and having minimal  involvement from all those involved with  it these stories are clearer and more  concise the underlying themes of Kingdom  Hearts harmonize with those of Disney's  own property so well that each new world  that saw her journeys to delivers an  impactful moment of storytelling  admittedly some of the stories retread  old grounds from the movies but whether  it's tangled pirates of the carribean  Winnie the Pooh Monsters Inc or Hercules  experiencing them again through the lens  of Kingdom Hearts 3 still packs an  emotional punch it's hard not to get  swept up in the exaggerated displays of  heroics or earnest reminders that your  friends exist in your heart one of the  strengths of Kingdom Hearts 3 is the  care and attention it pays to bringing  Disney's worlds to life which in turn  makes being in them all the more  exciting you get to wander around andis  bedroom as a diminutive toy version of  Sora scaling his walls and jumping on  his toys before making a trip to the  mall venture into the Pirates of the  Caribbean world and the game adopts a  striking realistic visual style and  gives you command of your own ship with  Jack Sparrow at your side San fransokyo  makes great use of verticality and  Sora's ability to effortlessly run up  buildings and glide between rooftops  while Monstropolis has you working with  Sully and Mike to stop Randal seizing  control of monsters ink and all the  while boo adorably Potter's around next  to you many of the walls offer extra  gameplay activities to engage with after  the story within them is wrapped up toy  box puts you in a mech and toss you with  destroying enemies in chasing high  scores Twilight town has a cooking  minigame which involves collecting  ingredients and bringing them to  ratatouille is Remy to make meals off  Pirates of the Caribbean lets you sail  the open sea or defend Port Royale in a  wave based minigame the amount of  gameplay in Kingdom Hearts 3 is  impressive and although the extras may  be short-term distractions for those who  want to spend more time in their  favorite worlds they're a fun reason to  make the return trip no awards maintain  that high bar as some feel either empty  or lacking in what they offer arendelle  snow-covered terrain for example feels  quite bland and the main mission  involves climbing a mountain more per  times portrayal is an entire location  used primarily for an item hunt toy  boxes Maul is devoid of life beyond the  toys and enemies  it would have been nice to have people  around to make it feel more alive  instead of like an after-hours shopping  center the same can be said of San  fransokyo which on ground level feels  eerily deserted for a metropolis the  bulk of Kingdom Hearts fries gameplay  however is in the sword-swinging magic  conjuring combat which feels fast  frenetic and spectacular in its  cinematic flourishes its most striking  feature is its fluidity Sora moves  between enemies quickly delivering a  barrage of attacks seamlessly  transitioning into casting spells  there's a pleasing sense of forward  momentum to all the bowels as you zip  around dispatching enemies in quick  succession  there are numerous layers on top of the  basic combat mechanics which while not  adding a great deal of depth or  strategic considerations make for more  exciting skirmishes keyblades now come  in a variety of flavors and have form  changes which transform them into more  over-the-top versions where more  powerful attacks and abilities become  available magic works similarly with  repeated use of a spell eventually  making a grand magic version available  and no additional mana cost throughout  Donald and Goofy will call to Sora for a  team-up attack these are characters that  have fought many battles side by side so  having these back and forth and  combination attacks are a nice  representation of the camaraderie  between them and their growth across the  series feeding into the Disney milieu  further our attractions such as tea cups  water offs bumper cars and a roller  coaster that can be summoned to dish out  damage each one controls differently  either through timed button presses  using the analog stick to guide their  path or becoming a first-person shooter  to pinpoint specific enemies they all  inject a different style of combat  gameplay into the action at regular  intervals  other Disney characters such as Simba  stitch and Ariel can be called into  bowel functioning similarly to Final  Fantasy summons to unleash devastating  special attacks the inclusion is  welcomed in lieu of giving them their  own worlds as some had in past games  beyond that this flow motion which  builds a sense of speed by encouraging  you to dash into objects in the  environment to swing around or at walls  to parkour along it can be tricky to get  a handle of but once you're able to work  these moves into the flow of combat you  build a sense of powers over the  battlefield watching the battles unfold  you'd be forgiven for thinking that the  combat is a complicated dance of fingers  across buttons but Kingdom Hearts 3 is  simple to play which works in its favor  it prioritizes spectacle above all else  and delivers tremendously that's not to  say it's completely devoid of strategic  considerations but you'll need to play  on the harder proud difficulty if you  want the game to challenge you otherwise  barring a few endgame bosses the enemies  are pushovers another feature that makes  this return from Kingdom Hearts of old  is the gummi ship while gummi ship  segments in the past were on Rails this  time you have full freedom to fly  wherever you please space is littered  with treasures to find but you'll often  have to battle enemies to acquire them  the shooting in the gummi ship segments  while serviceable isn't satisfying the  combination of lackluster visual and  auditory feedback makes it hard to tell  whether you're actually doing any damage  and for the most part I found myself  absent mindedly holding the fire button  and waiting for things to explode  as the game reaches its conclusion the  ballot is heavily in favor of non-disney  worlds with a main story of Kingdom  Hearts can play out and resolve itself  many of the environments this happens in  or striking from pristine white cities  to strange modular arenas that can be  turned upside down at the whim of an  enemy but in these locales the game  trades the heart and whimsy of the walls  up until that point for heavy-handed  storytelling that inevitably communism  battles there are cheap and spammy to  play the payoff meanwhile isn't entirely  worth it as Kingdom Hearts 3 wraps up  its story in an incredibly unfulfilled  way but the story of Keyblade Wars  time-traveling villains body hopping  also-rans and world ending darkness  isn't what I'll remember about Kingdom  Hearts 3 all the series as a whole what  sticks with me is the exciting battle  against an element or tie-in with  Hercules taking Rapunzel out into the  unfamiliar wide world for the first time  snapping selfies with Winnie the Pooh  and going toe-to-toe with Davy Jones in  2002 as Sora  I left destiny islands to travel across  the universe and make new friends in  2019 I brought all one's home and I had  so much fun doing it  just keep at it and I know you'll be  stronger than ever yeah I might even end  up stronger than you are  [Music]  [Music]  you

